//! check: run(exit=0, stdout="ignore_one_zero=invalid\nignore_one_kill=invalid\nignore_one_stop=invalid\nignore_one_two_bits=invalid\nignore_one_past_table=invalid\ndefault_one_zero=invalid\ndefault_one_kill=invalid\ndefault_one_stop=invalid\ndefault_one_two_bits=invalid\ndefault_one_past_table=invalid\nexit_zero=invalid\nexit_two_bits=invalid\nexit_past_table=invalid\nfar_host_number: true")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: os.signal.disp.one, os.signal.exit, err.union
//!
//! s246 (wolf-lang#783, #784; ruling asked, recommendation implemented) —
//! the rows of one meaning's disposition and of the end by a signal that
//! are decided by their SHAPE, before any host is asked: one truth on
//! every host, and nothing changes. A meaning is one bit of the table or a
//! host number -N, never 0; `KILL` (1048576) and `STOP` (2097152), which
//! no process can catch or ignore, are `invalid` for the dispositions. A
//! host number far past any host's last signal is `invalid` where the host
//! has numbers and `unsupported` on windows, which has none. The live
//! witnesses — a group send of a fault the sender ignores, a program that
//! ends itself by one — are `crates/wolf_driver/tests/signal_gaps_lanes.rs`.
