 A program that starts children has to find out when one of them changes.
-`os_wait_poll()` never waits. It looks at every child this program
-started and has not yet seen end, and answers `(h, status)` for the
-first one that ended or stopped since it last looked: the exit code, 0
-to 255, for a child that exited; `-N` for one ended by host signal `N`;
-and `256 + N` for one **stopped** by host signal `N` (`stop()` or a
